From d4b1ba6c259a9aa68c8eee7a1733d49f62eb25e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:54:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wallguard: the tables build again; TIF is Medium; the page
 says why blocking cannot work

The router's busybox flock has no wait option (it takes -s -x -u -n only), so
every Wallguard build and fold lock failed at once: no table was ever built
and the page kept saying the lists were downloading. wallguard.sh now polls
flock -n (lock_wait: 300 s for a build, 10 s for a fold); Warden's four
counter locks in rwarden.c had the same flaw and poll the same way.

The HaGeZi Threat Intelligence preset fetches the Medium list. The full one
(43.5 MB, about 2.1 million names) is past the per-list size and the table's
name limit and could never load; the preset keeps its id and bit.

A list download that Warden's router-traffic filter drops (a picked country,
the ban list or a threat feed) now names Warden, the country or list and the
server's address - in the log, the state file and the list's row on the
page - with the three ways out. The page also warns when a NAT rule sends
devices' DNS straight to another server (a Service Intercept rule, DNS
Director): those lookups never reach dnsmasq, so Wallguard and Dreadwatch
cannot see them. The build log reports the table's total, not the last
list's count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
